{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"earthly-wraithlike-urson","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Discovered during the DC↔Cloud test-parity re-audit (epic 3e73-72b5-cff2-40f0). DC guards that status is NEVER edited as a field: test_dc_outbound_status_routing_5200.py::test_the_dc_transport_never_edits_status_as_a_field. Cloud routes status via transition (src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py:162-183 pops status before 'workitem edit') and forwards it (test_update_one_forwards_status_to_client), but no test pins that 'status' never reaches the workitem edit field set. Gap: add a cheap structural guard that Cloud update_issue dispatches status via transition_issue and never includes it in the workitem edit payload. Test-only. Acceptance: add the regression guard.","id":"6194-8815-8ebb-42d0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Cloud outbound status never edited as a field (parity guard with DC test_dc_outbound_status_routing_5200)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785864424073313001,"uuid":"23ee82a4-5b18-4f07-9c6c-ee95e46dc27d"}